WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.133
Video twenty-one. Payroll.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.686
Payroll has five steps.

00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:09.166
First the masters: the employees and the pay
heads.

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:13.514
Then each month: the attendance, the payroll
voucher and the pay slips.

00:00:13.814 --> 00:00:19.966
Alter, Employee, Ramesh Patel. The employee
has a date of joining and the salary details.

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:28.765
The pay heads are the earnings and the deductions: Basic
Salary, House Rent Allowance, EPF and ESI.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:35.726
Press V, then Ctrl+F4 for payroll, and Ctrl+F5
for attendance.

00:00:36.427 --> 00:00:41.513
Ctrl+F opens Attendance Autofill. Select
Present, and type 26 days.

00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:47.231
Ctrl+A fills both employees, and Ctrl+A again
saves the attendance voucher.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:57.133
Ctrl+F4 opens the payroll voucher. Ctrl+F opens
Payroll Autofill: the salary for October.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:04.619
Ctrl+A computes each employee. Each pay head shows its
rule: a flat rate, or 12% of the basic for EPF.

00:01:04.649 --> 00:01:07.265
Ctrl+A saves the payroll voucher.

00:01:08.738 --> 00:01:12.354
Alt+G, pay slip: the net pay of each employee.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:23.690
Enter shows the pay slip of Ramesh Patel: earnings
₹21,000, deductions ₹1,913, net pay ₹19,087.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:28.920
Of ₹21,000, Ramesh gets ₹19,087.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:33.133
The EPF and the ESI go to the PF and ESI
funds.

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.151
Next video: backup and restore.

